    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0174" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">341.115 St 2/37½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: I quite agree with you
                    that the only course to take in the matter of the tank steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Brindilla</hi> and in other similar cases is to make an
                    immediate and vigorous protest against the action of the British authorities in
                    seizing an American vessel bound to a neutral port.</p>
                <p>In haste</p>
                <p>Cordially and faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
